Build PhysX 5.6.1 as a recipe-controlled, optionally GPU-accelerated package.

This bundles every source adjustment the recipe needs into one patch, applied
unconditionally in source(). The GPU-related hunks are inert in a CPU-only build
(cmakegpu/CMakeLists.txt is only INCLUDEd when PX_GENERATE_GPU_PROJECTS is on,
and the cudamanager driver-API code is compiled only for GPU builds), so there
is no need to guard them on the gpu option.

Changes:
* PIC control: drop PhysX's global SET(CMAKE_POSITION_INDEPENDENT_CODE ON) and
  the per-target POSITION_INDEPENDENT_CODE TRUE properties, so the recipe
  toolchain decides PIC via CMAKE_POSITION_INDEPENDENT_CODE.
* windows/CMakeLists.txt: honor PX_COPY_EXTERNAL_DLL instead of forcing the
  PhysXDevice/freeglut DLL copy via PUBLIC_RELEASE (the freeglut path is unset
  in this build and otherwise fails configure).
* Stop treating warnings as errors (/WX on Windows, -Werror on
  linux/mac/android/ios); modern toolchains emit far more warnings than PhysX's
  suppression lists cover.
* PxPreprocessor.h: don't force consumers to define exactly one of NDEBUG/_DEBUG.
* CUDA 12 -> 13 (GPU only): PhysX 5.6.1's GPU sources target the CUDA 12
  toolkit/ABI; bridge them to the CUDA 13 toolkit we build with (CUDA 13, unlike
  12.x, supports the very new host MSVC/GCC toolsets):
  - cmakegpu/CMakeLists.txt: drop -Werror=all-warnings (nvcc otherwise promotes
    modern MSVC STL <cmath> host/device diagnostics to fatal errors).
  - CudaContextManager.cpp: cuCtxCreate became _v4 in CUDA 13, taking an extra
    leading CUctxCreateParams* (passed NULL).
  - CudaKernelWrangler.cpp: PhysX ships its own cudart shim (PhysXGpu links only
    the driver); CUDA 13's generated fatbin registration references
    __cudaGetKernel/__cudaLaunchKernel, absent from the CUDA-12-era shim -- add
    no-op stubs matching the existing ones.

